{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>But if it is a vow or a freewill offering.</b> If he did not bring it on account of thanksgiving for a miracle, it does not require bread, and it is eaten for two days as is explained in the matter." "<b>And on the morrow, and what remains of it</b> on the first day <b>shall be eaten.</b> This vav is superfluous, and there are many like it in Scripture, such as ״וְאֵלֶה בְנֵי צִבְעוֹן וְאַיָּה וַעֲנָה״ (Genesis 36), ״תֵּת וְקֹדֶשׁ וְצָבָא מִרְמָס״ (Daniel 8)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:22.002027570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}